# Circle — environment template.
#
# Copy this file to `.env.local` and fill in real values:
#   cp .env.example .env.local
#
# `.env.local` is gitignored. NEVER commit real keys. NEVER hardcode them in source.
# On Vercel, set the same variables under Project Settings -> Environment Variables.

# --- Supabase (Phase 0) ---------------------------------------------------
# Supabase dashboard -> Project Settings -> API
# "Project URL" and the "anon / public" key. Both are safe to expose to the
# browser (that is why they carry the NEXT_PUBLIC_ prefix); Row Level Security
# is what protects the data, not the secrecy of this key.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=your-project-url
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-anon-key

# --- Not used yet; listed so the shape is known ---------------------------
# Phase 1+: server-only key that bypasses Row Level Security. Never expose to
# the browser, never prefix with NEXT_PUBLIC_. Used by migrations, the nightly
# reconciliation job, and the weekly keep-alive Action.
# SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=your-service-role-key
#
# Phase 4: Telegram bot token (BotFather).
# TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN=your-telegram-bot-token
#
# Phase 5: Gemini free-tier API key for the reminder agent.
# GEMINI_API_KEY=your-gemini-api-key
